The Qt6 example is in ../examples/ivyqt (see its README.md).

It uses the C++23 API in cpp/ivy.hpp and cpp/ivy_thread.hpp, linked with
ivy-cpp. ivy::LoopThread runs the native Ivy loop in a dedicated thread.
The GUI and demo workers send directly through the MT-safe ivy::Bus API;
incoming data and completion notifications reach the GUI through queued Qt signals.

The example's normal close path requests stop, waits for completion notifications
while Qt continues to run, and joins the producers before destroying the Bus.
There is no IvyContextIdle polling or native Qt socket/timer backend in this example.
See ../QT6_INTEGRATION.md for the optional future QtCore backend study.
